GitHub Actions: https://github.com/boop-bip80/operating-system-1/actions
Each phase's CI run publishes its available build and test evidence as an
artifact, including failed runs. Artifacts have a 14-day retention period;
download evidence needed for a lasting release/review record.

Kernel provenance and licensing
-------------------------------

This repository retains the Linux kernel source tree. The Phase 1 starting
point is commit 1c542b368c25323551c74278e64a886ed0c6f129 on rcu-free-v3;
its Makefile identifies Linux 7.3-rc7. New builds record the exact source
commit actually built rather than treating this historical baseline as HEAD.
The release-candidate kernel and virtual-machine test coverage are not a
production stability or hardware-qualification guarantee.

The distro scaffolding is isolated in distro/phase1/, distro/phase2/, and
distro/phase3/, and generated files
are kept out of the kernel source directories. The root kernel Makefile is
unchanged by the Phase 1 orchestration.

See COPYING, LICENSES/, and Documentation/process/license-rules.rst for the
Linux kernel's GPL-2.0 terms, syscall exception, and per-file licensing.
BusyBox, Debian packages, Weston, Sway/wlroots, GtkLayerShell, GRUB and OVMF
retain their own license obligations;
source versions, checksums, and redistribution notes are recorded in
docs/os/BUILD_PROVENANCE.md. Preserve these notices when redistributing.

Upstream kernel documentation: https://docs.kernel.org/
Kernel build instructions: Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst
